From 62b08999c2902c1a948976cf102d516d307e6a8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:26:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban workers: lean skills index + compact
 kanban_show payload

A dispatcher-owned Kanban worker re-reads its whole system prompt on every API call, and the first
tool result of every run is kanban_show. Both carried bytes a worker never uses.

1. Skills index (`skills.index_in_kanban_worker: full|compact|names`, default compact). Only when
   `owned_kanban_task()` is set: `compact` drops each row's `Asks:`/`Not for:` trigger text (it
   matches a user's own phrasing; a worker has a card, not a user), `names` demotes every category
   to a names-only line. No mode hides a skill name. Chats keep the full index. Snapshot v7 rows
   carry the exact `triggers` suffix so a cold start strips it without re-parsing SKILL.md, and the
   LRU key carries the mode.
2. kanban_show (dispatcher worker, no `verbose=true`): drops `capacity_evidence` and
   `execution_observations` (`capacity_note` keeps the one-line reading), collapses consecutive
   same-run heartbeat/dispatch_skipped/respawn_guarded/wake_episode_evidence rows into the newest
   one with `repeated`/`first_at`, strips `_`-prefixed internal payload keys, and replaces every
   text of 64+ bytes that `worker_context` already carries verbatim (`task.body`, comment bodies,
   run summary/error/metadata) with "(in worker_context)"; a text the context caps (8 KB body,
   2 KB comment, 4 KB run field) or tail-drops stays whole. `verbose=true` returns the old payload;
   interactive and orchestrator callers are unchanged.

Card: t_01a1dadad13bd037 (follow-up of t_01a1d975f8eb8e3f).
